<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of Canudos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a>–<a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of Canudos was a conflict between the Brazilian Republic and the religious community of Canudos in the backlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a>, founded by the preacher Antônio Conselheiro. The settlement, which grew to many thousands of poor followers, defeated three military expeditions in 1896–1897 before a fourth, much larger force destroyed it in October 1897, killing most of its inhabitants. Euclides da Cunha described the war in Os Sertões.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-canudos.jpg" alt="War of Canudos" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Rsabbatini at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canudos-map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
